{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For a remembrance.</b> For the generations." "<b>And you shall feast it.</b> The day that is for you a remembrance — that you feast. And we have not yet heard which is the day of remembrance; Scripture says, ״זָכוֹר אֶת הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה אֲשֶׁר יְצָאתֶם״ (Exodus 13) — this teaches us that the day of the Exodus is the day of remembrance. And which day did they go out? Scripture says, ״מִמָּחֳרַת הַפֶּסַח יָצְאוּ״ (Numbers 33) — you would say the fifteenth of Nisan is the festival day, for on the night of the fifteenth they ate the paschal offering and in the morning they went out (Mekhilta)." "<b>Throughout your generations, etc.</b> Might I hear a minimum of two generations? Scripture says, ״חֻקַּת עוֹלָם תְּחַגֻּהוּ״ (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:37.967244756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}